            <ArticleTitle>Comparison between videodensitometric and angiocardiographic determination of left ventricular ejection fraction in patients with cardiac disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angiocardiograms have been widely used to calculate volumes of cardiac chambers. By determining the left ventricular volume in end-diastole and end-systole the ejection fraction can be calculated. The ejection fraction is considered a clinically useful index of left ventricular function and is widely used in the preoperative evaluation of patients with cardiac disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
